{"links":[{"id":"af928051c403","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":35,"p":[36,36],"r":[3,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. iii. 10, 13."},{"id":"77400f2595fe","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":35,"p":[37,37],"r":[3,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. iii. 14, 15."},{"id":"a68b1e0fb39c","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":35,"p":[40,40],"r":[3,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. iii. 10."},{"id":"e102f9b9bea3","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":35,"p":[41,41],"r":[3,13],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. iii. 13."},{"id":"5f619f135f13","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":76,"p":[23,23],"r":[2,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. ii. 9, 10."},{"id":"bc91a4a742db","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_jo","w":"chrysostomus.hom_jo","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":41,"p":[7,7],"r":[2,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. ii. 4"},{"id":"47e29c461f7d","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_jo","w":"chrysostomus.hom_jo","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":41,"p":[7,7],"r":[2,11],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. ii. 11"},{"id":"11b3964f06ad","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":34,"p":[5,5],"r":[3,13],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mod. text omits this clause relating to St. Paul, as in the old text it is incomplete, the remainder of the sentence (\"would not have been wroth,\" etc.) having been transposed to the end of what relates to Barnabas, after \"relating to the decree.\"-Below, alla lambanousin eautouj , may perhaps be eautoij , sc. touj deomenouj below, i.e. choose their spheres of action where each was most needed. But the context rather seems to require this sense: \"There is no animosity between them, but they take their parts in this dispute for the good of those who, as Mark, need the instruction which was to be derived from the gentleness of Barnabas, and the severity of Paul's character. Paul indeed is stern, but his object is to do good: as 2 Thess. iii. 13, where (comp. the context) rebuking, and enjoining severity to be shown to the disorderly, he says, \"And be not weary in well-doing.\" We have changed the order of the two sentences, \"And he rebukes,\" etc. and, \"As he does elsewhere,\" etc.- Touto kai en th sunhqeia poioumen . i. e. this putting on a show of anger, to do good to one whom we would correct: or perhaps, of altercation, as when, for instance, father and mother take opposite parts, the one for punishing, the other for sparing an erring child- sunaganakthsai tw IIaulw . Ben. indignati esse in Paulum. But whether it means this, or \"to have had indignation together with Paul,\" there is nothing to show: nor is it clear what is the reference of the following sentences; unless it be, But he would not allow these persons who were indignant along with, or at, him, to retain this feeling: he takes them apart, makes them see the thing in its right light, and so departs in peace, \"being commended by the brethren to the grace of God,\" with the prayers of concord and charity. Great is the power of such prayer. (See the former comment on this verse, p. 214.)- Kau uper megalou acioij, kan anacioj hj . Perhaps it should be h , \"Whether it be on behalf of a great man (as Paul), or whether the person be unworthy,\" etc."},{"id":"d9c6e5d5ca8b","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":13,"p":[36,36],"r":[1,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. i. 6"},{"id":"43c7cf05e525","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":31,"p":[32,32],"r":[1,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. i. 9"},{"id":"455ec58294c2","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":32,"p":[1,1],"r":[3,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. iii. 6"},{"id":"7f1650596ba6","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_eph","w":"chrysostomus.hom_eph","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":13,"p":[9,9],"r":[1,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. i. 6"},{"id":"47a7e117a1c3","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_eph","w":"chrysostomus.hom_eph","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":22,"p":[33,33],"r":[2,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. ii. 7"},{"id":"31479a4f6800","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1th","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1th","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":11,"p":[4,4],"r":[2,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. ii. 2"},{"id":"88f5c638016b","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_2th","w":"chrysostomus.hom_2th","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[0,2],"r":[1,1,1,2],"k":"sectionCommentary","m":"editionHeading","c":"high","cited":"2 Thessalonians i. 1, 2","note":"Abschnittsangabe der Ausgabe zu „Homily 2“"},{"id":"074739416c24","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_2th","w":"chrysostomus.hom_2th","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[0,2],"r":[1,9,1,10],"k":"sectionCommentary","m":"editionHeading","c":"high","cited":"2 Thessalonians i. 9, 10","note":"Abschnittsangabe der Ausgabe zu „Homily 3“"},{"id":"ab5344ec0cb9","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_2th","w":"chrysostomus.hom_2th","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[0,2],"r":[2,6,2,9],"k":"sectionCommentary","m":"editionHeading","c":"high","cited":"2 Thessalonians ii. 6-9","note":"Abschnittsangabe der Ausgabe zu „Homily 4“"},{"id":"bdef5912c944","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_2th","w":"chrysostomus.hom_2th","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":5,"p":[0,2],"r":[3,3,3,5]